{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And a man — his holy things shall be his.</b> Since the priestly and Levitical gifts were stated, one might think they could come and take them by force — therefore Scripture says, ״וְאִישׁ אֶת קֳדָשָׁיו לוֹ יִהְיוּ״ — this teaches that the benefit of enjoyment belongs to the owners. And many more midrashim were expounded on it in the Sifrei; and another interpretation: ״וְאִישׁ אֶת קֳדָשָׁיו לוֹ יִהְיוּ״ — whoever withholds his tithes and does not give them, to him the tithes shall be: in the end his field yields only one-tenth of what it had been accustomed to yield. (Tanhuma Re'eh)" "<b>A man who gives to the priest.</b> The gifts that are owed to him." "<b>To him it shall be.</b> Much wealth. (Berakhot 63a)"], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:09:29.140586713Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}